            "review_title": "Review at Hanoi Terrace Cafe",
            "review_text": "pink00flamingo\nLondon, United Kingdom210 contributions\n0\nBest restaurant in the area\nJan 2019 • Solo\nI saw this place whilst I was on the tourist hop-on-hop-off bus and luckily I was able to get off at the Opera House and eat here. I wanted to eat traditional Vietnamese food but in a clean, social place and not have to pay a lot of money. There are a few levels to the restaurant, with the first floor offering great views over the area and of the opera house. The menu is really good as are the cocktails and fresh smoothies. I also bought one of the banana cakes to take away and it was the best I ate my whole 2 weeks in the country. Imagine local street food served and presented high class style. Amazing tastes and quality.\n\nThe staff were all really friendly and the ones that spoke very good English looked after me and gave me some travel tips. The restaurant was quite busy with locals whilst I was there which I took as a very good sign. One of the groups told me this was their regular hang-out for iced-coffee and cakes which is quite common in Vietnam. Will definitely come back here when I'm next in Hanoi.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 14, 2019",
            "rating": 1.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
